<section id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Instruction</h4>

<div id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following CoE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, we directly reuse the evaluation instructions provided in their work to ensure consistency and professionalism.Specifically, the instructions used for each dataset are listed in figs <a href="#Ax4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Instruction ‣ Implementation ‣ C. Experiment Details ‣ D2HScore: Reasoning-Aware Hallucination Detection via Semantic Breadth and Depth Analysis in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> - fig <a href="#Ax4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Instruction ‣ Implementation ‣ C. Experiment Details ‣ D2HScore: Reasoning-Aware Hallucination Detection via Semantic Breadth and Depth Analysis in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ax4.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11569v1/figures/gsm8k_instruction.png" id="Ax4.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/343;" width="698" height="343" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>The instruction used to prompt LLMs for GSM8K and MGSM datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Ax4.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11569v1/figures/mmlu_instruction.png" id="Ax4.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/343;" width="698" height="343" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>The instruction used to prompt LLMs for MMLU dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Ax4.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11569v1/figures/belebele_instruction.png" id="Ax4.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/343;" width="698" height="343" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>The instruction used to prompt LLMs for Belebele dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Ax4.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11569v1/figures/theoremqa_instruction.png" id="Ax4.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:698/996;" width="698" height="996" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>The instruction used to prompt LLMs for TheoremQA dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Inference</h4>

<div id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We set the maximum output length to 1024 tokens and used the <span id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;eos_token&gt;</span> for truncation. The inference process employs greedy decoding without random sampling. All the models we used are 7B/8B, thus in the all experiments we use 2 RTX4090.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Baselines</h4>

<div id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the mathematical definitions of the seven baseline uncertainty metrics used in our evaluation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ax4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Maximum Softmax Probability</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks and Gimpel 2017</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Reflects the model’s confidence by averaging the maximum predicted probability at each decoding step:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{MaxProb}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}[\max\mathbf{p}_{t}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>MaxProb</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{MaxProb}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}[\max\mathbf{p}_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Perplexity</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Si et al. 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Approximates the weighted branching factor of a language by exponentiating the average negative log of the maximum predicted probability:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PPL}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}[-\log(\max\mathbf{p}_{t})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>PPL</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PPL}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}[-\log(\max\mathbf{p}_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. 2025</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Measures the average distributional uncertainty across the sequence:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Entropy}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[-\log\mathbf{p}_{t}\right]\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Entropy</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Entropy}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[\mathbb{E}\left[-\log\mathbf{p}_{t}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temperature Scaling</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shih, Sadigh, and Ermon 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before applying softmax to logits <math id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}=(z_{t,1},z_{t,2},\ldots,z_{t,|V|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}=(z_{t,1},z_{t,2},\ldots,z_{t,|V|})</annotation></semantics></math> at each decoding step <math id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
we divide them by a temperature parameter <math id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> to calibrate the output distribution:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{t}^{(T)}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{t}}{T}\right),\quad\text{i.e.}\quad p_{t,i}^{(T)}=\frac{\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,i}}{T}\right)}{\sum_{d=1}^{|V|}\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,d}}{T}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>i.e.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{t}^{(T)}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{t}}{T}\right),\quad\text{i.e.}\quad p_{t,i}^{(T)}=\frac{\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,i}}{T}\right)}{\sum_{d=1}^{|V|}\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,d}}{T}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we set <math id="Ax4.I4.i4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>.
Subsequent calculations are consistent with Maximum Softmax Probability:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Temperature Scaling}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[\max_{i}p_{t,i}^{(T)}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Temperature Scaling</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Temperature Scaling}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[\max_{i}p_{t,i}^{(T)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Energy</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2020</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Maps logits to an energy value as a substitute for softmax-based confidence. At each step <math id="Ax4.I4.i5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the energy is computed as:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Energy}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[-T\cdot\log\left(\sum_{d=1}^{|V|}\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,d}}{T}\right)\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Energy</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Energy}=\mathbb{E}_{1\leq t\leq T}\left[-T\cdot\log\left(\sum_{d=1}^{|V|}\exp\left(\frac{z_{t,d}}{T}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I4.i5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="Ax4.I4.i5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CoE-R</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2025</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A confidence score computed by averaging the difference between relative magnitude and relative angle changes across adjacent hidden states.</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CoE-R}(H)=\frac{1}{L}\cdot\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\left(\frac{M(h_{l},h_{l+1})}{M(h_{0},h_{L})}-\frac{A(h_{l},h_{l+1})}{A(h_{0},h_{L})}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>CoE-R</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CoE-R}(H)=\frac{1}{L}\cdot\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\left(\frac{M(h_{l},h_{l+1})}{M(h_{0},h_{L})}-\frac{A(h_{l},h_{l+1})}{A(h_{0},h_{L})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I4.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I4.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I4.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CoE-C</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. 2025</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let each transition from layer <math id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l+1</annotation></semantics></math> be a complex number <math id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, where its magnitude is <math id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{l,l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{l,l+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and its angle (argument) is <math id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{l,l+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{l,l+1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{l}=M_{l,l+1}e^{iA_{l,l+1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{l}=M_{l,l+1}e^{iA_{l,l+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I4.i7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The CoE-C score is then the magnitude of the average of all these complex numbers:</p>
<table id="Ax4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CoE-C}(H)=\left|\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}C_{l}\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>CoE-C</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CoE-C}(H)=\left|\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}C_{l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.SSx2.SSSx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the mathematical formulations of the three evaluation metrics used in our study.</p>
<ul id="Ax4.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUROC (Area Under Receiver Operating Characteristic)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sets of positive and negative samples, and let <math id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the confidence score of sample <math id="Ax4.I5.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">AUROC measures the probability that a randomly chosen positive sample has a higher score than a randomly chosen negative one:</p>
<table id="Ax4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AUROC}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}||\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}}\mathbb{1}(s_{i}&gt;s_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>AUROC</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AUROC}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}||\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}_{\text{pos}}}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}}\mathbb{1}(s_{i}&gt;s_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I5.i1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ax4.I5.i1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FPR@95 (False Positive Rate at 95% Recall)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">FPR@95 is the false positive rate at the threshold where recall reaches 95%.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ax4.I5.i2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> be the threshold such that:</p>
<table id="Ax4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\ast}=\arg\min_{\tau}\left|\text{Recall}(\tau)-0.95\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>τ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Recall</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\ast}=\arg\min_{\tau}\left|\text{Recall}(\tau)-0.95\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I5.i2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then:</p>
<table id="Ax4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FPR@95}=\frac{\text{FP}(\tau^{\ast})}{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>FPR@95</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>FP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FPR@95}=\frac{\text{FP}(\tau^{\ast})}{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{neg}}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax4.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AUPR (Area Under Precision-Recall Curve)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Ax4.I5.i3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> be a threshold. Define:</p>
<ul id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TP}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TP}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>: true positives with <math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FP}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>FP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FP}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>: false positives with <math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FN}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>FN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FN}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>: false negatives with <math id="Ax4.I5.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then:</p>
<table id="Ax4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Ax4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Precision}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Precision</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Precision}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}(\tau)}{\text{TP}(\tau)+\text{FP}(\tau)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}(\tau)}{\text{TP}(\tau)+\text{FP}(\tau)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Ax4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Recall}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Recall</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Recall}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Ax4.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}(\tau)}{\text{TP}(\tau)+\text{FN}(\tau)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>TP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>FN</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{TP}(\tau)}{\text{TP}(\tau)+\text{FN}(\tau)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Ax4.I5.i3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">AUPR is the area under the precision-recall curve:</p>
<table id="Ax4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AUPR}=\int_{0}^{1}\text{Precision}(r)\,dr," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>AUPR</mtext><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mtext>Precision</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AUPR}=\int_{0}^{1}\text{Precision}(r)\,dr,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax4.I5.i3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Ax4.I5.i3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\text{Recall}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Recall</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\text{Recall}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> varies with the threshold. This is computed via numerical integration.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ax5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">D. Additional Figures</h2>

<div id="Ax5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To support the visualization of token dispersion patterns in the Method Section, we present some representative examples used in our dispersion’s visualization analysis: as shown in fig <a href="#Ax5.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ D. Additional Figures ‣ D2HScore: Reasoning-Aware Hallucination Detection via Semantic Breadth and Depth Analysis in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> - <a href="#Ax5.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ D. Additional Figures ‣ D2HScore: Reasoning-Aware Hallucination Detection via Semantic Breadth and Depth Analysis in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ax5.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11569v1/figures/hallucination_example.png" id="Ax5.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:698/1461;" width="698" height="1461" alt="Refer to caption">
